iser","type":{"id":"508","text":"Blocked","abbreviation":"shot-blocked"},"clock":{"displayValue":"2:49"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"4"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"4587985","displayName":"Mark Kastelic","shortName":"M. Kastelic"},"type":"shooter"},{"athlete":{"id":"4697717","displayName":"Wyatt Kaiser","shortName":"W. Kaiser"},"type":"defender"}]}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"1824","guid":"58cac4d0-a208-3028-b2a6-ff7aba657bc3","fullName":"TD Garden","address":{"city":"Boston","state":"MA","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1824.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":17850,"officials":[{"fullName":"Kelly Sutherland","displayName":"Kelly Sutherland","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Matt MacPherson","displayName":"Matt MacPherson","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Jonathan Deschamps","displayName":"Jonathan Deschamps","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Liam Maaskant","displayName":"Liam Maaskant","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Lindholm's overtime goal lifts the Bruins past the Blackhawks as Pastrnak moves past Bergeron","description":"— Elias Lindholm scored in overtime as the Bruins rallied from a two-goal deficit in the third period to top the Chicago Blackhawks 5-4 and extend Boston’s home winning streak to five games.","story":"BOSTON -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3041994/elias-lindholm\">Elias Lindholm</a> scored in overtime as the Bruins rallied from a two-goal deficit in the third period to top the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/chi/chicago-blackhawks\">Chicago Blackhawks</a> 5-4 and extend Boston’s home winning streak to five games.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697461/mason-lohrei\">Mason Lohrei</a> scored to pull Boston within a goal and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4268466/morgan-geekie\">Morgan Geekie</a>'s second goal of the season with 12 seconds left in the third period sent the game into overtime.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5080227/ryan-greene\">Ryan Greene</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5149125/connor-bedard\">Connor Bedard</a> scored in the third period as the Chicago Blackhawks took a 4-2 lead. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5291935/anton-frondell\">Anton Frondell</a> had his second career two-goal game for Chicago.\n\n\r\n              The Blackhawks came into the game with the worst power play in the NHL, converting on 4 of 40 opportunities and were 0 for 11 on the power play on the road. However, it took Frondell just 11 seconds to give Chicago the lead after <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3941946/will-borgen\">Will Borgen</a> was whistled for a delay-of-game penalty.\n\n\r\n              Goaltender <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4392765/michael-dipietro\">Michael DiPietro</a> kept Boston in the game with key saves as the Bruins were outshot 28-13 in the first two periods. He stopped a Bedard shot from the slot with 2:09 left in the first period. Geekie, who hasn't scored in his previous nine games, hit a shot off the post late in the first period.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3114778/david-pastrnak\">David Pastrnak</a> scored on a breakaway in the first period for his 428th career goal, passing Patrice Bergeron and moving into sole possession of third place on the Bruins’ career goal-scoring list. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4233575/casey-mittelstadt\">Casey Mittelstadt</a> and Mason Lohrei also scored for the Bruins.\n\n\r\n              Frondell redirected <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3042056/tyler-bertuzzi\">Tyler Bertuzzi</a>'s wrist shot from the point past a surprised DiPietro early in the second period for his second career two-goal game. DiPietro, coming off his <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/predators-bruins-score-9325e23d963f904f142a66e011aed5e1\">first career NHL shutout</a>, kept it a one-goal game with a point-blank save of 500-goal scorer <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3735/patrick-kane\">Patrick Kane</a> midway through the second period. The Bruins tied the game when Mittelstadt took a feed from James Hagen and snapped a shot past <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4894729/arvid-soderblom\">Arvid Soderblom</a>.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Blackhawks: Host Avalanche on Monday.\n\n\r\n              Bruins: Host Vegas on Monday.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-10-31T20:31:46Z"}}